      MD: { name: 'Maryland', days: 45, kind: 'cal', trigger: 'termElseVacate', daysRule: '45 calendar days after the end of the tenancy, plus accrued interest of at least 3% yield. If repair costs cannot be determined in time, the landlord must send a written estimate — nothing can be withheld without it.', statute: 'Md. Code, Real Prop. §8-203', url: 'https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-203',
        statement: 'Written itemized statement of deductions with the balance; skipping the estimate provision forfeits the right to withhold.',
